      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Occult Catharsis",
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "emotion",
        "healing",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "Krohan's magic converts his pain into spellpower. After he casts an innate occult spell, he attempts a DC 5 Flat check, increasing the DC by twice the spell's rank if it was not a cantrip. On a success, Krohan's Spirits Drawn to Suffering effect ends; he can reduce the value of one condition affecting him by 1, and he regains 2d6 healing Hit Points."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Spirits Drawn to Suffering",
      "actions": "free",
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per 10 minutes\n\nTrigger Krohan critically fails a saving throw, takes mental damage, takes damage from a critical hit, or gains a harmful condition with a numerical value (such as frightened or sickened). This effect does not trigger due to self-harm or similarly engineered circumstances.\n\n---\n\nEffect Krohan gains the ability to cast his innate occult spells for 1 minute.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "PT10M"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Unwitting Rivethun",
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "emotion",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "Krohan has very limited access to Rivethun magic, able to cast spells only when experiencing pain or distress."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Righthand Man",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "Krohan gains a +2 circumstance bonus to attack rolls and skill checks attempted to Aid others. He can attempt a Dwarf Lore check in place of any other attack roll or skill check to Aid a dwarf.",
